00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:58.100
And I can make this offset V.

267
00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.679
I want to make sure that both of these are on.

268
00:10:59.679 --> 00:11:04.980
So make sure the one is on for each.

269
00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.320
There we go.

270
00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:07.740
But to be able to be able to do,

271
00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.720
to get this to work correctly, I should say,

272
00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.120
to be able to be able to do this,

273
00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:18.059
we want to use a thing called a append vector.

274
00:11:18.059 --> 00:11:23.500
So I'm going to type in append vector.

275
00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.440
What this does,

276
00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.580
it allows us to be able to actually

277
00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.279
have a secondary control.

278
00:11:29.279 --> 00:11:32.399
And we can pipe this into an add or multiply.

279
00:11:32.399 --> 00:11:36.120
So I can grab this UV offset, plug it into each channel,

280
00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:40.470
grab this offset here and plug it into the B channel.

281
00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.549
And now if I want, I can choose,

282
00:11:42.549 --> 00:11:46.500
let me hit the hotkey A and left click and add,

283
00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:50.200
hit my finger with the M key and left click or multiply.

284
00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.759
Now the difference between these, if I did add,

285
00:11:52.759 --> 00:11:55.600
things would shuffle and stay pretty linear,

286
00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:59.090
straightforward with no size changes.

287
00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:00.830
And I'd have to connect this here

288
00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:03.840
and have to connect this here.

289
00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:06.919
Or if I want, I can do multiply.

290
00:12:06.919 --> 00:12:09.639
And I prefer multiply because it scales it a little bit

291
00:12:09.639 --> 00:12:11.600
and can maybe hide some of the imperfections

292
00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.080
after the texture.

293
00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.960
So I can pull this into the A channel

294
00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.879
and pull this into the B channel.

295
00:12:16.879 --> 00:12:18.480
And then I grab each one of these

296
00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.820
and put it into the UV slots for each one.

297
00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:25.139
And then I hit apply.

298
00:12:25.139 --> 00:12:26.240
With those plugged in,

299
00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:28.639
we're going to make sure that you hit save.

300
00:12:28.639 --> 00:12:30.610
I just hit apply.

301
00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:31.970
And then now we look at our instance

302
00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:36.799
and you'll see we have UVs all ready to go.

303
00:12:36.799 --> 00:12:40.840
Now again, each one of these should be in a group.

304
00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.879
I didn't do it because just to save time

305
00:12:42.919 --> 00:12:44.679
that we went over in the first class,

306
00:12:44.679 --> 00:12:46.879
but you can now see down here, the UV,

307
00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.659
the offset U, the offset V,

308
00:12:51.659 --> 00:12:57.789
and you'll see it scaling and then the overall tiling.

309
00:12:57.789 --> 00:13:01.169
So again, using that and the multiply or the add

310
00:13:01.169 --> 00:13:03.690
can determine how that's going to shuffle.

311
00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.840
And I can show you really quick.

312
00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.519
I go in here and then switch this to an add

313
00:13:09.519 --> 00:13:14.080
for both of these and then apply.

314
00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.710
We can now go into here and change things.

315
00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.100
And you'll notice it's a lot linear.

316
00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:23.000
There's no stretching going on.

317
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.720
Now it does make it so it repeats more.

318
00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:28.220
So it squishes it, but the other way around,

319
00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:31.000
multiply has a little bit more of a scale connected to it.

320
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.679
Well, that's it with this lesson.

321
00:13:32.679 --> 00:13:33.559
In the next lesson,

322
00:13:33.559 --> 00:13:37.000
we're going to take a look at creating masked materials.
